            <ArticleTitle>Periostin: a new extracellular regulator of obesity-induced hepatosteatosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>562-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2014.09.005</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(14)00402-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Periostin is a crucial extracellular remodeling factor in the inflammatory and tumor microenvironments, but its function in nonalcoholic fatty liver disease remains unclear. Lu et al. (2014) now demonstrate that periostin is a critical player in the regulation of hepatic triglyceride homeostasis and the development of obesity-induced hepatosteatosis.</AbstractText>
